Pull images by digest from a build manifest.

A tag can be pushed again, so a deployment pulling by tag may run images
other than the ones its deployer was built and tested with: a node added
months later, or a pull during a publish window, gets whatever the tag
names at that moment. A containerised deployer image can say exactly
which images it was built with.

When the deployer image carries a build manifest,
/etc/kolla-ansible/manifest.json (kolla_image_manifest_path), naming the
digest of every image built with it, each image it names is now pulled
by digest:

    {"format_version": 1, "tag": "<build tag>",
     "images": {"nova-api": "sha256:<hex>", ...}}

Each key is the image's repository within docker_namespace, that is the
kolla-build name with any docker_image_name_prefix, so a manifest still
applies when the images are mirrored unchanged to another registry.

Every <service>_image_full now resolves through a new kolla_image_full
lookup plugin, whose rules are in kolla_ansible/image_manifest.py. It
returns <image>@<digest> when the manifest names the image and the
image's tag is the manifest's tag, and <image>:<tag> otherwise, so an
overridden <service>_tag, an image outside docker_registry and
docker_namespace, and an image the manifest does not name, such as
rabbitmq-upgrade.yml's versioned RabbitMQ image, are pulled by tag as
before. A lookup, unlike a filter, can read the play's variables, so the
variables need not repeat the registry, namespace and manifest path. The
parsed manifest is cached by path, and re-read only if the file changes,
because these variables are templated on every use.

The deployer checks also check the manifest. A deployer image without
one warns once, and pulls every image by tag. A manifest built with a
tag other than the deployer's is refused unless
--override-deployer-checks is given. A manifest which cannot be read, or
whose format_version is not understood, fails both the checks and the
lookup, whatever the override, because pulling by tag is what the
manifest exists to prevent; pointing kolla_image_manifest_path at a path
which does not exist pulls by tag instead.

Switching a deployment between tag and digest references changes every
container's image, so every container is recreated once. The release
note says so.

This depends on kolla_container accepting digest references with
Docker, which an earlier change in this series adds.

